#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""The World in One Day - Monday 23 November 2026.

A program that draws one newspaper front page summing up the world's news
of Monday 23 November 2026: 40 verified stories, 13 of them highlighted
with a drawn picture each, a world map with a numbered pin for every story,
a UTC timeline, stat boxes, and an honest date check.

Standard library only.  The typefaces (Playfair Display Bold for the
masthead and headlines, Liberation Serif for body copy, Liberation Sans
Bold for labels) are baked in below as 4-bit grayscale coverage bitmaps
that were rendered from the font files at build time; at run time the
program only decodes those bitmaps and blits them onto an RGB buffer.
No Pillow, no network, no timestamps, no randomness: two runs write
byte-identical PNGs.

Layout (1024 x 1024, black and white with a sparing gold accent):
  top band, masthead, kicker line, UTC timeline strip, stat boxes,
  region bar, 13 highlight cards (3 large, 10 small), the world map
  beside the 27 further stories, a DATE CHECK box and a HOW WE CHECKED
  footer.  Every text box is sized from measured wrapped text.
"""

